rt \\(|T_n|=n(n+1)/2\\) and the explicit value of \\(f(n)\\).\n\n*If \\(n=2m\\) is even:* \\(f(n)=m\\). Then  \n\n\\[\nt\\ge\\frac{m(2m+1)-2m\\cdot m}{2m-m}\n      =\\frac{m}{m}=1 .\n\\]\n\nThus at least one non‑sunny line is necessary, i.e.  \n\n\\[\ns\\le n-1 .\n\\tag{10}\n\\]\n\n*If \\(n=2m+1\\) is odd:* \\(f(n)=m+1\\). Then  \n\n\\[\nt\\ge\\frac{(2m+1)(m+1)-(2m+1)(m+1)}{(2m+1)-(m+1)}=0 .\n\\]\n\nHence no non‑sunny line is forced; all \\(n\\) lines may be sunny:\n\n\\[\ns\\le n .\n\\tag{11}\n\\]\n\nConsequently any admissible covering must satisfy (10) when \\(n\\) is even and (11) when \\(n\\) is odd. These are the **necessary** restrictions on \\(k\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### Construction attaining every admissible \\(k\\)\n\nLet \\(k\\) be an integer satisfying the necessary bound:\n\\[\n0\\le k\\le n\\ \\text{if }n\\text{ is odd},\\qquad\n0\\le k\\le n-1\\ \\text{if }n\\text{ is even}.\n\\]\n\nSet \\(t=n-k\\) (the number of non‑sunny lines we shall use).\n\n1. **Non‑sunny part.**  \n   Take the vertical lines  \n\n   \\[\n   L_i:\\;x=i\\qquad (i=1,2,\\dots ,t).\n   \\]\n\n   These \\(t\\) lines are distinct, non‑sunny, and together cover all points of\n   \\(T_n\\) whose first coordinate does not exceed \\(t\\).\n\n2. **Remaining points.**  \n   The points not yet covered are  \n\n   \\[\n   U=\\{(a,b)\\in T_n\\mid a\\ge t+1\\}.\n   \\]\n\n   Write \\(a'=a-(t+1)\\) (so \\(a'\\ge0\\)). Then the condition \\(a+b\\le n+1\\) becomes\n   \\(a'+b\\le n-t\\). Hence \\(U\\) is exactly the translate by \\((t+1,0)\\) of the set\n   \\(T_{n-t}\\).\n\n3. **Sunny covering of \\(U\\).**  \n   By Lemma 1 the set \\(T_{n-t}\\) can be covered by  \n\n   \\[\n   \\Bigl\\lceil\\frac{|T_{n-t}|}{f(n-t)}\\Bigr\\rceil\n   =k\n   \\]\n\n   sunny lines (the equality follows from (9), which is an equality when we\n   substitute \\(t=n-k\\)).  \n   An explicit family is as follows.\n\n   *If \\(n-t\\) is odd, write \\(n-t=2r+1\\).  \